{
 "label": "EXPLORATORY: S2 hedge event study, March 2024 market data (Bybit prints, Binance best bid/ask), v1_6 entry rule and frozen S1 table, ASSUMED delays 45 ms, unwind band 15 bps ASSUMED; no simulator fill, no HOLDOUT",
 "rules": "(1) TRAIN 2024-03-01..03-07 chooses, SELECT 2024-03-08..03-11 confirms; HOLDOUT is never read (this wrapper refuses any day after 03-11). A split with fewer than 30 eligible events is flagged TOO_FEW_TO_COMPARE and nothing is chosen from it.\n  (2) The TRAIN choice is the variant with the lowest MEAN cost after fees over ALL events (unwound chains included, so a tight cap cannot look cheap by dropping its failures). Variants within 0.02 bps of the best tie; a tie goes to the lower unwind rate, then to the\n      lower 99th-percentile cost. The 95th and 99th percentile costs are reported for every variant.\n  (3) SELECT confirms the choice when its SELECT mean cost is no higher than today's cap (slack5) on SELECT by more than 0.02 bps AND its 99th-percentile cost is no more than 2 bps above slack5's on SELECT. If the TRAIN winner is not confirmed, today's cap (slack5) stays.\n  (4) If a break-even cell is the TRAIN winner and is confirmed on SELECT: a core change request is written to port it to the session runtime. If not: the break-even cap is recorded as DROPPED.",
 "assumptions": {
  "d_send_s": 0.045,
  "d_report_s": 0.045,
  "d_unwind_s": 0.035,
  "backoff_s": 0.25,
  "retries": 2,
  "unwind_band_bps": 15.0,
  "size": 1.0,
  "maker_bps": 1.0,
  "hedge_taker_bps": 1.7,
  "maker_venue_taker_bps": 3.2,
  "max_walk_bps": 2.0,
  "min_gap_s": 1.0,
  "fill_rule": "an improving quote is filled when the sweep prints at least our size; a quote joining the touch when the sweep prints at least the displayed touch size plus our size (no cancellations: conservative)",
  "label": "ASSUMED delays (no measured Binance delay exists); Binance March-2024 is best bid/ask only: the hedge size is assumed to fit at the touch"
 },
